  "result": "```json\n{\n  \"smpl.ordering.repositories.mongodb.models.CatalogItem\": {\n    \"summary\": \"MongoDB persistence model for catalog items in the ordering system. This class serves as a data mapper between the domain model (smpl.ordering.models.CatalogItem) and MongoDB storage. Annotated with @Document to map to the 'catalog' collection. Key fields include an @Id annotated 'id' for MongoDB document identification, an @Indexed 'skuNumber' for efficient querying, along with description, price, inventory, and leadTime. Provides bidirectional conversion: a constructor that accepts a domain CatalogItem object to create a MongoDB document, and a toCatalogItem() method that converts back to the domain model. The toCatalogItem() method includes business logic to calculate lead time dynamically - setting it to 0 when inventory is available (inventory > 0), otherwise using the stored leadTime value. This class follows the Repository pattern, acting as the persistence layer representation of catalog items.\",\n    \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/repositories/mongodb/models/CatalogItem.java\"\n  }\n}\n```",
